speechtext:
It runs through the northern section of the Rainy River dis-tiict. The route is given in section 8 of the charter, chapter 152 of the Statutes of 1910:
Prom a point on the northern boundary of the state of Minnesota at or near the town of Fort Prances, to a point on the lake of the Woods at or near the mouth of Big Grassy river;
From a point on the said line west of the township of Mather, to a point on the lake of the Woods at or near the mouth of the Little Grassy river;
From a point, or points, on the first described line in or east of the township of Mather, to a point on the northern boundary of the state of Minnesota at or near the Long Sault rapids on the Rainy river, and to the town of Rainy River or a point on the northern boundary of the state of Minnesota at or near the town of Rainy River.

There is now no
protection for shipping going to Hudson bay. The inauguration of the Hudson Bay railway of necessity -involves tremendous expenditure iby this Government in order to provide for the navigation of the bay and the strait. My hon. friend in administering the Department of Railways has found that supplies for the bay have to be transported in vessels from the Maritime provinces;

and the safety of those vessels and the control of the territory lying between the strait of Belle Isle and the Hudson strait are matters of great importance.

One of the contractors came to Ottawa on the 30th of March. I have seen him since then, and he told me that he had received a letter stating that he was liable to forfeit his deposit. There must be some understanding, as the contractors seemed anxious to keep the contract and would have kept it had they been allowed to do so.
There was a question of having a dredge on the work, but I understand that the engineer in charge advised the contractors that the work could be done with a dredge;

but a dredge could not be procured at that time as all were at work for the season. There was nothing left but to do the work by -day labour, and they worked in that way for some weeks. I am surprised that they did not get an extension of time, because I saw them last week, and they seemed anxious to do the work.
